    <description>Screen subflow used to deploy an assigned asset or cancel a shipment.
Captures deployment details, creates a Deployed Asset Assignment record, and updates the Asset status and current assignment.

2026-07-30: INC3-91 Phase 3 - Deploy path no longer creates Asset_Assignment__c directly. Removed Create_Assignment_Records; added Update_Deployed_Asset which stamps Status=&quot;Deployed&quot;, Status_Change_Notes__c=&quot;Deployed via Manage Asset console&quot;, and Deployment_Date__c directly on the Asset, triggering Asset_After_Create_Assignment_on_Status_Change to create the assignment and stamp Current_Assignment__c. This also fixes a pre-existing bug: Deployment_Date__c was previously assigned to variable assignmentToCreate but a different, always-blank variable assetAssignmentToCreate was what actually got passed into the legacy subflow, so Deployment_Date__c was never really saved on the assignment record. TODO(L8): the &#39;Cancel Shipment&#39; radio choice on the Deployed Info screen has never been wired to any branching logic - flow always proceeds to Deploy regardless of selection. Pre-existing issue, out of scope for this migration.</description>
